---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="Advisory for Large-Scale Mining & Exploration Companies"
  description="Helping large-scale mining and exploration companies find land responsibly and manage the interface with artisanal and small-scale mining."
>
  <section class="section service-page">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="eyebrow"><a href="/what-we-do">&larr; What We Do</a></p>
      <h1 class="reveal">03 &middot; Advisory for Large-Scale Mining &amp; Exploration Companies</h1>
      <p class="lede reveal">
        Large-scale concessions in Sub-Saharan Africa rarely sit in
        isolation from artisanal mining, and exploration, including the
        current wave of exploration chasing cobalt, lithium, copper and
        other transition minerals, rarely starts on genuinely empty
        ground. We support both ends of that timeline.
      </p>

      <div class="body-grid">
        <div class="reveal">
          <h2>What this covers</h2>
          <p>
            For exploration-stage companies: land search and ground
            assessment that accounts for existing artisanal activity,
            customary land claims and community presence before a
            concession boundary is drawn.
          </p>
          <p>
            For operating concessions: mapping artisanal mining activity in
            and around the site, assessing the safety, legal and
            reputational exposure it creates, and designing coexistence or
            formalisation pathways that reduce conflict at its source.
            Community relations work where an LSM operation and ASM
            livelihoods overlap, and incident response support when that
            relationship has already broken down and needs to be rebuilt.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="reveal">
          <h2>How we work</h2>
          <p>
            We operate our own ASM site, which gives us credibility on both
            sides of this relationship: artisanal miners recognise us as
            fellow practitioners, and LSM operators get advice grounded in
            how an ASM operation actually functions day
            to day.
          </p>
          <p>
            Recommendations are built around what a concession can
            realistically implement and sustain, given its existing
            security, community relations and compliance structures.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="cta-row">
        <a class="pill-btn" href="/contact">Talk to us about your concession</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>

<style>
  .service-page .eyebrow {
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
  }

  .lede {
    max-width: 720px;
    font-size: 1.1rem;
    margin-bottom: clamp(2rem, 4vw, 3rem);
  }

  .body-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    gap: var(--gap);
    margin-bottom: clamp(2.5rem, 5vw, 4rem);
  }

  .cta-row {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
    padding-top: 2rem;
  }

  @media (max-width: 800px) {
    .body-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
  }
</style>
